  "root_cause": "The update_product function updates the database and invalidates only the shared cache layer by calling invalidate_shared(product_id), but it does not invalidate the local cache layer (stored in _local). As a result, subsequent get_product calls may retrieve stale data from the local cache, causing outdated product data to be returned despite updates.",
  "code_commitments": [
    "update_product must invalidate local cache after update",
    "update_product must invalidate shared cache after update"
  ],
  "fix_strategy": "Add a call to invalidate_local(product_id) within update_product after updating the database, ensuring both cache layers are invalidated and subsequent reads fetch fresh data.",
